       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
      * EXEC SQL in DB2's conventions (docs/esql.md, phase 2): INCLUDE
      * SQLCA (built in), DECLARE ... TABLE, CONNECT ... USER :host, a
      * host structure for INSERT and SELECT INTO, an indicator taking
      * a NULL, SQLERRD(3) as the rows touched, WHENEVER NOT FOUND and
      * SQLERROR each going to a paragraph, and CONTINUE.  No oracle:
      * GnuCOBOL has no precompiler of its own.
       PROGRAM-ID. DB2STYLE.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
           EXEC SQL INCLUDE SQLCA END-EXEC.
           EXEC SQL DECLARE EMP TABLE
             (EMPNO CHAR(6) NOT NULL, ENAME VARCHAR(20),
              SALARY DECIMAL(9,2)) END-EXEC.
       01  EMP-REC.
           05 EMPNO    PIC X(6).
           05 ENAME    PIC X(20).
           05 SALARY   PIC S9(7)V99 COMP-3.
       01  NAME-IND    PIC S9(4) COMP.
       01  USERID      PIC X(8) VALUE "PAYROLL".
       01  CNT         PIC S9(9) COMP.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-PARA.
           EXEC SQL CONNECT TO DB1 USER :USERID END-EXEC
           EXEC SQL WHENEVER SQLERROR GO TO SQL-ERR END-EXEC
           EXEC SQL CREATE TABLE EMP
             (EMPNO CHAR(6) NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
              ENAME VARCHAR(20), SALARY DECIMAL(9,2)) END-EXEC
           MOVE "000010" TO EMPNO MOVE "HAAS" TO ENAME
           MOVE 52750.00 TO SALARY
           EXEC SQL INSERT INTO EMP VALUES (:EMP-REC) END-EXEC
           DISPLAY "INSERT SQLCODE " SQLCODE " ROWS " SQLERRD(3)
           EXEC SQL INSERT INTO EMP VALUES ('000020', NULL, 41250)
           END-EXEC
           EXEC SQL UPDATE EMP SET SALARY = SALARY * 1.1 END-EXEC
           DISPLAY "UPDATE ROWS " SQLERRD(3)
           MOVE SPACES TO EMP-REC
           EXEC SQL SELECT EMPNO, ENAME, SALARY INTO :EMP-REC
             FROM EMP WHERE EMPNO = '000010' END-EXEC
           DISPLAY "GOT [" EMPNO "] [" ENAME "] " SALARY
           EXEC SQL SELECT ENAME INTO :ENAME :NAME-IND FROM EMP
             WHERE EMPNO = '000020' END-EXEC
           DISPLAY "NULL NAME IND " NAME-IND
           EXEC SQL WHENEVER NOT FOUND GO TO NONE-FOUND END-EXEC
           EXEC SQL SELECT COUNT(*) INTO :CNT FROM EMP WHERE 1 = 0
           END-EXEC
           EXEC SQL SELECT ENAME INTO :ENAME FROM EMP
             WHERE EMPNO = '999999' END-EXEC
           DISPLAY "NOT REACHED"
           STOP RUN.
       NONE-FOUND.
           DISPLAY "NOT FOUND, SQLCODE " SQLCODE " STATE " SQLSTATE
           EXEC SQL WHENEVER NOT FOUND CONTINUE END-EXEC
           EXEC SQL INSERT INTO EMP VALUES ('000010', 'DUP', 1)
           END-EXEC
           DISPLAY "NOT REACHED EITHER"
           STOP RUN.
       SQL-ERR.
           DISPLAY "SQLERROR " SQLCODE " " SQLSTATE " [" SQLERRMC "]"
           EXEC SQL WHENEVER SQLERROR CONTINUE END-EXEC
           EXEC SQL COMMIT END-EXEC
           STOP RUN.
